  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "ZfrO67fyThrgtBZk7mC5FBvawWA=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:27.112Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Camunda IDP is documented as using *\"artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) to identify, extract, and organize data from your structured and unstructured documents\"*. The ABBYY partnership of 19 December 2025 delivers an ABBYY Vantage connector for *\"classification, extraction, validation, and human-in-the-loop capabilities\"*.\n\nBoth are real, both shipped in the stated window, and neither has any bearing on whether Camunda keeps an immutable attributed log of business decisions. \"Document\" in Intelligent Document Processing means a scanned invoice; \"document\" in a document-model platform means a typed state machine. The two senses share a word and nothing else.\n\nThe practical warning is about screening method: a vendor announcement can occupy the same vocabulary as your thesis without occupying the same slot. Anyone who ruled Camunda out on this basis ruled it out for the wrong reason \u2014 and would have missed that the gap actually did close, elsewhere, in release 8.9.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T08:45:27.112518Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:27.112526Z"
    }
  },
